<p>I don't think there is a lot of fertile ground left for the whole &quot;antimeme&quot; thing but this article manages to provide the necessary subtlety in order to convey that there is a lot more going on here and the fact that it's not/can't be talked about is <em>attractive</em> for this piece.</p>
<p>This was enough content in a small enough space that I found it worth an upvote, but I feel that this would benefit from perhaps making the implications a little more profound (while preserving the vague). I know the foundation deemed this anomalous for reasons you stated, but to me there is an unstated suggestion here that it really might just not be. I like that. If that's me putting words into your mouth that you didn't intend, such is the beauty of the art of writing.</p>

